WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.402
A useful way to think about data cleaning is as evidence-based decision making.

00:00:05.402 --> 00:00:09.192
We begin by observing what is actually in the data.

00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:19.157
Before changing anything, count missing values, blank strings, invalid values, duplicates, and unusual values.

00:00:19.157 --> 00:00:23.008
We want to understand the problem before we try to solve it.

00:00:23.485 --> 00:00:27.802
Next, we decide what can be standardized using a documented rule.

00:00:27.802 --> 00:00:36.912
For example, if an email has extra spaces around it, removing those spaces does not change the meaning of the email

00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:40.042
address. That is a reasonable standardization.

00:00:40.042 --> 00:00:43.622
But we should also preserve the original evidence.

00:00:43.622 --> 00:00:47.417
A cleaned value is our interpretation of the source value.

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:50.367
It should not erase where the value came from.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:55.632
And finally, when we do not know the correct answer, we should not guess.

00:00:55.632 --> 00:01:01.337
A suspicious record can be flagged for review instead of being automatically changed.

00:01:01.337 --> 00:01:04.469
That mindset will guide the entire module.
